<MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Align="Align.Left">
    At brainboost we are constantly working on improving our Neurofeedback software: the BrainAssistant.<br/>

    <MudLink Href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neurofeedback" Target="_blank">Neurofeedback</MudLink> is a modern and recent method of neurotherapy.
    It can be used to a large variety of cases, from ADHD and ADD therapy to peak performance training.

    In general, Neurofeedback works by using an EEG amplifier to collect data on brain activity, analyzing these signal spectrums, and using this to control feedback applications.
    Signal spectrums are using bins commonly referred to as frequency bands, such as Theta (4-8 Hz), Alpha (8-12 Hz), and Low Beta (12-20 Hz).
    Different training protocols then aim to reduce the amplitude of measurements within specific frequency bands while increasing it within others.

    As such, you not only need EEG-capable hardware and a software tool to record & evaluate the data, but also actual training apps.
    For this, brainboost uses games developed in-house with Unity (or Flash for some of the original versions), which is where I came in when joining the company.
    My first major project was NeuroRacer (see below) and it was a great success with both our direct Neurofeedback clients as well as our business customers.
</MudText>
